# Line endings, stated explicitly instead of left to each machine's core.autocrlf.
#
# `desktop.cmd` must be CRLF in the working tree on every platform: cmd.exe misparses a batch
# file that uses bare LF (goto labels and parenthesised blocks break), and that failure looks
# like a broken project rather than a checkout setting. Without this file the ending depends on
# the cloner's `core.autocrlf`, so the same commit could run for one person and not for another.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Windows executables and other binaries must never be line-ending-translated.
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
